From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Leese <leese@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:26:45 -0700
Subject: [DevTools] Fix Local Overrides origin spoofing via CSS sourceURL
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fixes two issues that allowed a page to spoof local override paths in
DevTools via a crafted /*# sourceURL=... */ comment in a <style> tag:

1. StylesSourceMapping did not call NetworkProject.setSourceURLSynthesized
   on UISourceCodes created from stylesheet headers with hasSourceURL,
   allowing "Override content" to remain enabled in the context menu for
   synthetic CSS sourceURLs.

2. NetworkPersistenceManager.isForbiddenNetworkUrl returned false when
   ParsedURL.fromString failed to parse an un-normalized URL (such as
   "http://example.com /evil.css"), failing open instead of closed while
   encodedPathFromUrl still extracted a host/path from the string.

Also updates unit tests that passed schemeless URLs to
encodedPathFromUrl, and updates OverridesHelpers.createWorkspaceProject
to construct local file:/// override URLs directly from the file
relative override path rather than passing schemeless/forbidden paths
through fileUrlFromNetworkUrl.

Bug: 562233597
Change-Id: Icc115f33c5b2a3295a32c3b223940f26492d044b
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/devtools/devtools-frontend/+/8481965
Reviewed-by: Simon Zünd <szuend@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Eric Leese <leese@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
front_end/models/bindings/StylesSourceMapping.test.ts does not exist on this branch; its test-only hunk was dropped. Applied on top of the two upstream prerequisites (devtools-frontend c2153bf24a and 6c25c4672f) that introduced the forbidden-URL checks this fix extends.

